{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Construct sweep complete — 2 confirmed siblings fixed, landed for review (Gerrit 2342)\n\n**DISPOSITION: LANDED** (Gerrit change 2342, commit 498e484168316b9b548c322cd9877738ab5ab208) — awaiting Verified +1 + LLM-Review +1.\n\n### Sweep (Step 7 Axis 1) — every candidate site + disposition\nConstruct: a DETERMINISTIC shared temp name (f\"{self.path}.tmp\" / <hash>.tmp) followed by os.replace/Path.replace onto a shared final path, reachable by concurrent writers.\n\nCONFIRMED REAL SIBLINGS (fixed):\n- peer_confirmations.py PeerConfirmationStore.save() — shared .bridge_state/peer_confirmations.json; concurrent passes possible in the lease-steal/zombie-pass window (no abort_check before the persistence-phase save()). FIXED with per-writer tempfile.mkstemp.\n- impossible_links.py ImpossibleLinkStore.save() — identical construct on .bridge_state/impossible_links.json. FIXED identically.\nThese were the ONLY 2 of the reconciler package's 7 atomic-write sites not already on mkstemp — the same package standardized the other 5 (pass_io, binding_repository, apply_planning, get_rotation, last_pass), a decisive design-invariant signal these two were omissions.\n\nEXCLUDED (string-match candidates refuted semantically):\n- review_bot/reconcile.py _write_cursor — single sequential reconcile_loop asyncio task, single-box PoC; no concurrent writers.\n- _config_writer.py / _cli/__init__.py — one-shot config write.\n- _opcert_signing.py — temp is PID-unique and content byte-identical .pub; no lost-write hazard.\n- staging.py — uuid4-unique temp + write-lock.\n- All existing mkstemp/NamedTemporaryFile/fsutil sites, tests, and the two already-fixed files (Gerrit 2329 completion_verdict_cache.py, 2334 plan_review/sizing.py).\n\nOverlap-hint tickets checked (not duplicates): c1fd (closed; reducer _cache.py — different subsystem) and fea4 (closed; hardened projects_store.py bridge-state writes but left these two sidecars untouched — corroborates the gap).\n\n### Fix\nProven pattern from 2329/2334: unique tempfile.mkstemp(dir=..., prefix=..., suffix=\".tmp\") -> write via returned fd -> atomic os.replace onto the shared final path (last-write-wins preserved) -> on failure unlink only the writer's own temp, then fail open. Fail-open behaviour and McCabe complexity unchanged (no new branches).\n\n### Validation\n- RED->GREEN regression tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_bridge_state_atomic_write_concurrency.py (barrier at os.replace, one test per store).\n- Mutation check (sandboxed): reverting either site to the shared temp turns both tests RED (FileNotFoundError -> _dirty never cleared); unique temps GREEN.\n- Full apply suite: 264 passed (incl. AC8 fail-open no-regression).\n- make lint + make typecheck clean; C901 flat, files 359/396 LOC (well under the 800 cap).\n\n### Attribution\nOmission-class (--class=preexisting): caused_by -> 248f-ac00-18db-4259 (peer_confirmations, commit c638bc6) and b8b1-6462-b4f1-4a1d (impossible_links, commit 54bdc0f); both predate the package's mkstemp hardening."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787952146279280001,"uuid":"4c0bec2f-b178-4a7c-aa36-9d5a3a773d39"}